  "historical_dependency_mapping": {
    "test_ordinary_relocated_minimal_tree_accepts_all_interfaces": "Both M0/M1 metadata and artifact positives use five explicit pinned byte snapshots with all source reads prohibited; no relocated filesystem tree is required by the new API.",
    "test_each_call_rechecks_missing_changed_oversized_and_nonfile_dependencies": "SnapshotContract tests each path and public API for missing/extra/exact key/value types/short/long/changed/oversize plus repeated-call validation; no cache can promote changed bytes.",
    "test_each_dependency_symlink_and_its_ancestor_symlink_fail_after_import": "Filesystem path acquisition is outside this bytes API. Original test remains unchanged. Exact string key/bytes admission plus no source opens replace this boundary here; no claim of new filesystem symlink validation.",
    "test_reparse_attribute_on_files_and_ancestors_is_rejected": "Same scoped replacement as symlink acquisition: no source-data rereads. Existing read-only module-location resolution is permitted. Original filesystem test stays intact.",
    "test_adapter_does_not_mutate_other_historical_consumers": "SnapshotContract tests M0/M1/M0 and sentinel historical sys.modules identities/globals; snapshots stay unchanged, results stay independent."
  },
  "adaptation_audit": [
    "Fifteen metadata and thirteen artifact test bodies preserve every existing direct assertion count; their shared fixtures now supply required explicit motors and exact snapshots. They are concrete source methods, not runtime text projections.",
    "Public constant checks now assert the normative ten flags/reference84/name24/flags5 rather than requiring undocumented subject constants.",
    "Diagnostic project negatives become app_motor_fault.ino because app.ino is now positive; rewritten path negative remains explicitly unequal.",
    "Both motor variants use coherent opposite-profile flags as a negative; PROBE=0 is changed to1. New case rejects reordered/missing/duplicate/extra/B4-disabled and each competing-profile macro across all matching properties.",
    "Seven filename aliases are identity mappings. The old legacy packet negative is explicitly renamed to app_motor_fault.ino; extra-name cases use diagnostic names rather than current positive aliases.",
    "Artifact expected report keeps all historical fields/nested layout/TLS/size/hash data, changes only outward status/project/flags/identity aliases and adds declared motors_allowed. Direct bad native/frozen/export calls supply required keywords through the same no-effect fixture.",
    "Every five-snapshot mutation is tested for each public API before exec. Motor failures are compared with the same invalid-motor baseline and forbid both source hashing and exec to establish motor admission ordering.",
    "Caller snapshot map is altered by a controlled callback at the first private exec; successful checks must use the earlier validated copy. Original bytes are immutable and not changed.",
    "All original33 historical tests and source files remain unchanged; five filesystem dependency tests are explicitly mapped above, not silently deleted or claimed applicable."
  ],
  "no_effects": "During subject import/public calls, builtins/io/Path source reads and writes, descriptor opens, subprocesses, sockets and filesystem mutations raise AssertionError. Read-only module-location resolution remains permitted. Historical synthetic/helper inputs are pinned and loaded only by test fixture setup.",
  "commands": {
    "linux_first": "env TMPDIR=/dev/shm python3 -I -B tests/tooling/test_b4_app_static_policy.py -v",
